WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Okay, so in this lesson we're going to talk about gradient descent.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Gradient descent is the algorithm that almost every neural network uses to learn.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
The basic idea is simple: we have a loss function that measures how wrong our model is,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
and we want to make that loss as small as possible.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:31.000
So we start with random weights, we compute the gradient of the loss with respect to the weights,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.000
and the gradient tells us the direction of steepest increase.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Since we want to decrease the loss, we take a step in the opposite direction of the gradient.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.000
The size of that step is controlled by a number called the learning rate.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:56.000
If the learning rate is too big, we might overshoot the minimum and never converge.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
If it's too small, training will be correct but very slow.
